    "cwe_ids": [],
    "description": "The Image and Playlist blocks built markup with `preg_replace()` using replacement strings that include block attributes, so backreferences such as `$1` in those values were expanded into the output. The blocks now use `preg_replace_callback()`.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.4 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 6.4.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by Ben Bidner of the WordPress Security Team.",
    "ghsa_id": "GHSA-2p22-wv7j-cvfv",
